Looking at the demos, the pattern seems to be: the background-colored grid contains objects; one color appears as exactly one object (the "template"), and a smaller object of another color has the same shape type (up to scaling/reflection) — that object gets recolored to the template's color (demo 1: small 6-shaped L → 0; demo 2: 8-pair → 2; demo 3: 1-shape → 5). In the test, color 2 forms a single L-shaped object (h5 + v4), and the 3-colored triomino at rows 1-2, cols 13-14 is a scaled/reflected L matching it (color 0's T-blob matches nothing). So the 3-triomino should become 2.

